# Harness Improvements Todo

## Context

Raidar `main` is the realized first evaluation-suite version and is still CLI-first, with no meaningful dashboard or frontend. `feat/autoresearch-v3` is the in-flight branch for automatic experiment iteration, benchmark/research-loop separation, and objective-led scenario improvement.

Reviewed sources:

- [Meta-Harness: End-to-End Optimization of Model Harnesses](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.28052)
- [AutoHarness paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.03329)
- [LangChain: Improving Deep Agents with Harness Engineering](https://blog.langchain.com/improving-deep-agents-with-harness-engineering/)
- [deepagents better-harness example](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/examples/better-harness)
- [AutoHarness repo](https://github.com/aiming-lab/AutoHarness)

## Findings

- Harness design is now a first-class optimization surface. Prompt, tool, middleware, context, and harness-code changes can materially improve outcomes without changing the base model.
- `feat/autoresearch-v3` is directionally correct. It already has the important control-plane shape: objective state, bounded loops, benchmark vs research-loop roots, mutation guards, promotion guards, and confirmation reruns.
- The biggest Raidar gap is not another loop abstraction. It is evidence ergonomics: trace capture, local trace payloads, train/holdout semantics, and operator visibility.
- AutoHarness should not be folded in wholesale. It is strongest as a governance/audit/session framework, while Raidar should remain benchmark-first.
- `better-harness` is useful as a research-loop pattern: bounded editable surfaces, proposer workspace, train/holdout/scorecard cases, and keep/discard decisions.

## Recommended Work

1. Add explicit `train`, `holdout`, and `scorecard` case splits to research-loop workflows.
2. Add an editable-surface manifest to autoresearch objectives and loop reports.
3. Convert loop artifacts into a decision ledger:
   - candidate diff
   - research summary
   - reviewer memo
   - governor verdict
   - promotion guard
   - confirmation guard
4. Persist trace references and local trace payload snapshots when available.
5. Add a thin operator surface over existing artifacts:
   - benchmark vs research-loop navigation
   - loop status table
   - blocked/unscored reasons
   - diff summary
   - promotion outcome
   - trace links
6. Keep promotion conservative:
   - no validity regressions
   - no frozen-metric regressions
   - no unscored candidate runs
   - confirmation rerun before promotion
   - bounded mutation surface remains enforced

## Capability Matrix

| Capability | Raidar `main` | Raidar `feat/autoresearch-v3` | deepagents `better-harness` | AutoHarness |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Scenario-contract eval suite | Strong | Strong | Weak | Weak |
| Repeatable benchmark runs / comparisons | Strong | Strong | Partial | Weak |
| Separate benchmark vs research-loop roots | Weak | Strong | Partial | Weak |
| Automated outer-loop iteration | No | Strong | Strong | No |
| Bounded editable / mutation surfaces | Partial | Strong | Strong | Strong |
| Explicit train / holdout / scorecard loop splits | No | No | Strong | No |
| Conservative promotion guards / confirmation reruns | Partial | Strong | Partial | No |
| Trace / artifact persistence for debugging | Partial | Partial | Strong | Strong |
| Governance / permissions / constitutions | Low | Low | Low | Strong |
| Operator dashboard / richer UI | Low | Low | Low | Strong |

## Implementation Bias

- Fold train/holdout/scorecard semantics, editable-surface manifests, and decision-ledger artifacts into `feat/autoresearch-v3`.
- Fold richer trace/evidence capture and the thin inspection surface into `main` once stable.
- Borrow governance ideas from AutoHarness only where they improve evaluation trust or safety. Do not convert Raidar into a general-purpose agent governance wrapper.
